; M3 gate: (trig N) music->game sync points. `(trig N)` emits TRIG (0x42) with
; an explicit id N (0..63); the driver records it in the track's game-readable
; status byte, id in bits 5-0 under a 2-bit firing counter. TRIG has no register
; effect, so the register trace does not see it.
;
; Two tracks fire distinct, sticky triggers at different beats; the byte holds
; (last-wins) until the next trigger. The same id firing twice is
; m4-trig-loop's case.
(fm1 :tempo 120 :alg 4 :fb 3 :ar1 31 :tl1 20 :ar4 31 :tl4 8 :len 4
  (trig 1) c d e f
  (trig 2) g a b > c
  (trig 63) < g)
(sqr1 :len 4
  c e (trig 10) g e
  c (trig 20) e g > c)
